Toward a Formal Theory of Beneficial Human–LLM Coupling: A Dynamical Systems Framework

From Cognitive Offloading to Cognitive Amplification

ouadi Maakoul 

AI: chatGpt, Claude, Gemini, Deepseek 

Abstract

This dissertation develops a mathematically explicit framework for characterizing conditions under which sustained interaction between a human and a large language model generates autonomous cognitive capability rather than substitutive dependence. The central theoretical object is a state-dependent dynamical system in which the critical variable is not immediate task performance under assistance but the long-term evolution of the human cognitive state vector.

The framework establishes: (i) a multidimensional capability state space grounded in cognitive theory; (ii) a Filippov-type discontinuous dynamical system in which generative and substitutive coupling are modeled as distinct vector fields separated by a critical manifold, with sliding dynamics derived via Utkin's equivalent control method; (iii) existence theorems for fixed points via Brouwer's theorem, with strict positivity established under explicit inward-pointing conditions; (iv) local asymptotic stability characterized through Lyapunov linearization and Lyapunov inequalities; (v) an infinite-horizon optimal control formulation with costate dynamics derived via Pontryagin's Maximum Principle, including projection operators for constrained controls; (vi) a Cognitive Scaffolding Index (CSI) defined as a bounded efficiency ratio with a derived reduced-order approximation; (vii) a regularized stochastic extension based on Itô diffusions and Freidlin–Wentzell large deviations theory; and (viii) falsifiable predictions distinguishing model-falsifying hypotheses from normative claims.

The framework is positioned relative to recent empirical and theoretical work, including CentaurBench, AIRIS, and population-level cognitive virus models. The central insight is formalized as a mathematical proposition: observed AI-assisted performance can increase while latent human capability decreases. This distinction between augmentation and amplification motivates a control problem fundamentally different from conventional AI optimization.

The mathematical status of each result is explicitly classified as theorem, conditional proposition, derivation, conjecture, or empirical hypothesis. This classification reflects a commitment to mathematical precision over rhetorical certainty.

