Appendix I: Glossary of Key Terms

· Generative regime ($\Omega^-$): Coupling regime where $\Lambda < \Lambda_c$; AI promotes internalization.
· Substitutive regime ($\Omega^+$): Coupling regime where $\Lambda > \Lambda_c$; AI substitutes for human capability.
· Critical manifold ($\mathcal{M}_c$): Boundary where $\Lambda = \Lambda_c$; separates the two regimes.
· Sliding domain ($\mathcal{M}_c^*$): Attractive subset of $\mathcal{M}_c$ where trajectories are trapped.
· Pseudo-equilibrium: Zero of the sliding vector field on $\mathcal{M}_c$; distinct from BEB.
· Boundary equilibrium bifurcation: Collision of a smooth equilibrium with $\mathcal{M}_c$ as a parameter varies.
· Cognitive Scaffolding Index (CSI): Fraction of assisted gain converted to autonomous capability.
· Reversibility ($R_C$): Ratio of post-AI-removal capability to pre-AI capability.
· Quasi-potential ($V$): Minimum action required for a rare noise-driven transition.
· Beneficial Coupling Set ($\mathcal{B}$): Set of states satisfying capability growth, bounded dependency, epistemic calibration, and reversibility.

